                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A basic idle game core equipped with an incredibly tedious autobattler system that you immediately automate fully and then just watch for half an hour before being allowed to make another input. Then once you reach a certain point it just sort of peters out because the devs did not bother to include any sort of end game, just a bunch of virtually unreachable \"gain 1000000 of [resource]\" achievements that seem to be the end goal.\n\nEdit: I should say, the in-game achievements mentioned above are [i]not[/i] the same as the Steam achievements. You can 100% the Steam achievements in a few hours at most, and should probably see the game as \"finished\" at that point without bothering with the in-game ones.",
